    "version": "1.5.0",
    "released": "2026-09-16",
    "notes": "Adds a third plan type, \"time\", for selling extra days on their own.\n\nUntil now a plan was either data (type 2) or a traffic top-up (type 1), so a\nuser whose gigabytes were fine but whose expiry was days away had to buy a\nwhole new subscription. The admin plan form now offers a third type with two\npricing modes: fixed bundles (7 days at one price, 30 at another) and a per-day\nrate where the user picks the number of days. Each time plan can be limited to\nchosen subscription plans, or left open to all of them.\n\nThe order pipeline is encoded, so a time plan is stored as an ordinary topup\npackage (type 1, bandwidth 0) carrying a marker in order_note, and checkout is\nthe panel's own - coupon, gateway, invoice and order history all unchanged. The\ndays are granted afterwards by bin/timeplans.php, scheduled every minute from\nTaskCommand, and timeplan_log keys on the order id so a grant happens once.\nA per-day purchase first mints a package row priced at N x the daily rate;\nthe same row is reused for the same N, so the count stays bounded.\n\nOn the user's subscription card an \"add time\" button appears beside \"add data\",\nbut only near the end of the subscription - within timeplan_visible_days\n(default 7), or up to timeplan_grace_hours (default 24) after it expired. Both\nsettings are edited in the time plan form.\n\nThe grace window needed one fix elsewhere: UserJob zeroes transfer_enable the\nmoment a plan expires, so buying days afterwards would have returned a working\naccount with no data. UserJob now records the remaining traffic in\ntimeplan_snapshot before wiping it, and the grant puts it back - only when the\nsnapshot still matches the expiry being extended.\n\nAdmin and user endpoints live in app/Patch/TimePlan.php, dispatched from\npublic/xmplus-patch.php (endpoint 1.2.0) ahead of its blanket admin check,\nsince the buying half answers ordinary users. Adds twenty-two localization keys\nto en_US, fa_IR and zh_CN, and migration 004 for the two new tables.",
